<% content_for :title, "On Others | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-others-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-others-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-others-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-others-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / ON OTHERS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>OTHER</span>
        <span>FUCKING</span>
        <span>PEOPLE.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-others-intro">
        YOU CAN'T CONTROL THEM.<br>
        YOU DON'T HAVE TO LIKE THEM.<br>
        YOU DO HAVE TO DEAL WITH THEM.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- THE PROBLEM -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-pink">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      01 / OTHER PEOPLE
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        THEY'RE GONNA<br>
        DO WHAT<br>
        THEY DO.
      </h2>

      <p>
        People disappoint us. Ignore us. Misunderstand us.
        Judge us. Annoy the absolute shit out of us.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes they're wrong. Sometimes we're wrong.
        Sometimes everybody involved is being a little fucking ridiculous.
      </p>

      <p>
        The problem gets bigger when somebody else's behavior starts
        controlling what happens inside your head for the rest of the day.
      </p>

      <div class="others-callout">
        <p>
          THEIR BEHAVIOR IS INFORMATION.<br>
          YOUR RESPONSE IS STILL YOURS.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CONTROL -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-yellow">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      02 / CONTROL
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHAT'S<br>
        ACTUALLY<br>
        YOURS?
      </h2>

      <div class="others-control-grid">

        <div>
          <p class="others-label">YOURS</p>

          <p>What you say.</p>
          <p>What you do.</p>
          <p>What you tolerate.</p>
          <p>Where you go.</p>
          <p>Whether you respond.</p>
          <p>Whether you stay.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="others-label">NOT YOURS</p>

          <p>What they think.</p>
          <p>What they say.</p>
          <p>Whether they understand.</p>
          <p>Whether they apologize.</p>
          <p>Whether they change.</p>
          <p>Whether they approve of you.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        You can influence another person.
        You can ask. Explain. Negotiate. Walk away.
      </p>

      <p>
        You cannot crawl inside their fucking head and operate the controls.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BOUNDARIES -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-purple">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      03 / BOUNDARIES
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        A BOUNDARY<br>
        IS ABOUT<br>
        YOU.
      </h2>

      <p>
        A boundary isn't a magic sentence that forces somebody else
        to behave the way you want.
      </p>

      <div class="others-before-after">

        <div>
          <p class="others-label">CONTROL</p>
          <p>YOU'RE NOT ALLOWED TO TALK TO ME LIKE THAT.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="others-label">BOUNDARY</p>
          <p>IF YOU TALK TO ME LIKE THAT, I'M ENDING THE CONVERSATION.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        The second one tells the other person what
        <strong>you</strong> will do.
      </p>

      <div class="others-callout">
        <p>
          A BOUNDARY WITHOUT AN ACTION<br>
          IS MOSTLY A REQUEST.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- EXPECTATIONS -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-black">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      04 / EXPECTATIONS
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        THEY DIDN'T<br>
        FOLLOW THE<br>
        SCRIPT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        We write invisible scripts for people all the time.
      </p>

      <div class="others-thoughts">

        <p>"THEY SHOULD KNOW."</p>
        <p>"THEY SHOULD HAVE TEXTED."</p>
        <p>"THEY SHOULD CARE MORE."</p>
        <p>"THEY SHOULD UNDERSTAND WHY I'M UPSET."</p>
        <p>"IF THEY CARED, THEY WOULD..."</p>

      </div>

      <p>
        Sometimes those expectations are completely reasonable.
        The problem is assuming the other person knows the script
        when nobody handed them a fucking copy.
      </p>

      <div class="others-question">
        DID I ACTUALLY<br>
        COMMUNICATE THIS —<br>
        OR DID I EXPECT<br>
        THEM TO KNOW?
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- TAKING IT PERSONALLY -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-pink">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      05 / TAKING SHIT PERSONALLY
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        MAYBE IT'S<br>
        NOT ABOUT<br>
        YOU.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Somebody is quiet. Somebody doesn't text back.
        Somebody seems annoyed. Somebody walks past you.
      </p>

      <p>
        Your brain can fill the empty space immediately:
      </p>

      <div class="others-thoughts">

        <p>"THEY'RE MAD AT ME."</p>
        <p>"I DID SOMETHING WRONG."</p>
        <p>"THEY DON'T LIKE ME."</p>
        <p>"THEY'RE IGNORING ME."</p>

      </div>

      <p>
        Maybe.
      </p>

      <p>
        Or they're tired. Distracted. Busy. Upset about something else.
        Thinking about lunch. Having their own shitty day.
      </p>

      <div class="others-callout">
        <p>
          DON'T TURN MISSING INFORMATION<br>
          INTO A FUCKING CONVICTION.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- JUDGMENT -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-yellow">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      06 / JUDGMENT
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        THEY DON'T<br>
        HAVE TO<br>
        GET IT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        People may have opinions about your diagnosis,
        addiction, sobriety, medication, recovery, mistakes,
        past, work, relationships, or how you're rebuilding your life.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some criticism contains useful information.
        Some criticism is somebody else's fear, ignorance,
        assumptions, or bullshit.
      </p>

      <div class="others-question">
        IS THERE SOMETHING<br>
        USEFUL HERE —<br>
        OR AM I JUST BEING<br>
        HANDED THEIR OPINION?
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ANGER -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-purple">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      07 / ANGER
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        BEFORE YOU<br>
        POP THE<br>
        FUCK OFF.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Anger can show up fast, especially when something feels
        disrespectful, unfair, rejecting, threatening, or dismissive.
      </p>

      <p>
        You don't have to pretend you're not angry.
        You also don't have to make every decision while the anger
        is sitting in the driver's seat.
      </p>

      <div class="others-pause">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>What actually happened?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>What did I assume it meant?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>What am I feeling underneath the anger?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Does this need a response right now?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>What outcome do I actually want?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- RESENTMENT -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-black">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      08 / RESENTMENT
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        HOW LONG<br>
        ARE THEY<br>
        LIVING RENT-FREE?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Somebody can hurt you once and then continue occupying your
        thoughts for weeks, months, or years afterward.
      </p>

      <p>
        Letting go of resentment doesn't require deciding what they did
        was okay. It doesn't require reconciliation. It doesn't require
        letting them back into your life.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes letting go simply means deciding you're done spending
        this much of your own fucking energy on them.
      </p>

      <div class="others-callout">
        <p>
          FORGIVENESS AND ACCESS<br>
          ARE NOT THE SAME THING.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- COMPASSION -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-pink">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      09 / COMPASSION
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        UNDERSTANDING<br>
        ISN'T<br>
        EXCUSING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        You can understand that somebody's behavior comes from their own
        fear, pain, insecurity, history, addiction, mental health,
        or general inability to get their shit together.
      </p>

      <p>
        That understanding may help you take their behavior less personally.
      </p>

      <p>
        It does not mean you have to tolerate behavior that harms you.
      </p>

      <div class="others-before-after">

        <div>
          <p class="others-label">COMPASSION</p>
          <p>I CAN UNDERSTAND WHY YOU'RE LIKE THIS.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="others-label">BOUNDARY</p>
          <p>AND I STILL DON'T HAVE TO PARTICIPATE IN IT.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PAUSE -->
  <section class="others-section others-section-yellow">

    <div class="others-section-number">
      10 / BEFORE YOU REACT
    </div>

    <div class="others-section-content">

      <h2>
        CHECK YOUR<br>
        FUCKING<br>
        STORY.
      </h2>

      <div class="others-pause">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>What happened?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>What do I know for a fact?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>What am I assuming?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>What part of this actually belongs to me?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Do I need a conversation, a boundary, distance, or nothing at all?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>What response will I still be okay with tomorrow?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="others-ending">

    <p class="others-ending-small">
      YOU DON'T CONTROL OTHER PEOPLE. THANK FUCK.
    </p>

    <h2>
      LET THEM<br>
      BE THEM.<br>
      YOU BE YOU.
    </h2>

    <p>
      Pay attention to what people show you.
      Set boundaries where you need them.
      Take responsibility for your side.
      Leave their side with them.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "others-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>